  "body": "<p>Hana enters the continuation as someone Ryvyt regards as a friend living in the tower near <a href=\"#larkhollow\">Larkhollow</a>. His suspicion that she and a guarding creature might be the same being is a theory, not an established identity.</p><h2 id=\"hana-tower-encounter\">The tower encounter</h2><p>A voice identified as Hana refuses to let the visitors discover what the tower keeps hidden. The small figure falls inert as a doll; a distorted presence appears, guardians Tik and Tok attack, and a larger attacking figure is subsequently called Hana. Oya, Ryvyt and Pelagia escape.</p><p>What the tower protects, who controls the doll, and whether all manifestations share a single identity remain unanswered. Sylvi Fernstep later claims Lady Hana is older than local accounts suggest, without supplying a verified age or origin.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Scene sources: <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1547789358554423308\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1547801694996267129\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1547802560797351956\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">3</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1547806699912564746\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">4</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1547811278511284405\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">5</a>, <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/1177270231513694249/1199083630354501673/1554710921967046697\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">6</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hana-return-and-death\">The return to the tower</h2><p>Ryvyt returned to Larkhollow looking for a friend. A report of his gift doll, blood and a message at Hana’s tree drew him toward the tower with Pin, Saelihn, Oya and Fenwick. Hana’s warnings changed between a familiar childlike voice and a more psychic presence. She said a mother had forbidden entry; the company did not establish who that mother was.</p><p>Inside, a larger figure identified as Hana held Oya and Pin with telekinesis. Saelihn warped them free, then fought to keep pressure off Fenwick and drive their attackers back. Ryvyt healed Saelihn after Hana clawed her. He also cast fire at Hana, asking forgiveness as she burned. Pin attacked another clockwork opponent. The narrator’s continuation explicitly establishes Hana’s death and the burned body; it does not assign a separate, certain killing blow to one adventurer.</p><p>Ryvyt blamed himself and wanted to bury her once their work was done. Pin offered help. The continuation does not yet show that burial. <a href=\"#return-to-hanas-tower\">Read the return to Hana’s tower →</a></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"hana-after-the-fight\">The questions left in her tower</h2><p>Ryvyt and Pin continued into the basement and upper floors. They found a damaged Tik, fragments of a stone inscription, nearly erased symbols and paintings described as Pilgrims of the Lanterns. A final roofless floor held a painting titled The Gardener Beneath the Moon, where the account stops.</p><p>The death of the figure called Hana resolves the immediate fight. It does not identify the mother, establish how the voice, doll and larger body relate, or identify the painted Gardener. Those questions survive the expedition’s latest scene.</p>\n",
